== Global routing experiments (Caravel die)
  ORFS applies ROUTING_LAYER_ADJUSTMENT only in floorplan.tcl, so
  pre_grt.tcl re-applies it at global route (runs before that change
  used the floorplan-time value).
  run                         adj   macro m1-m3 blk   result                      met2 use   wall
  iter (old RTL)              fp    no                3,431 gcells overflow (GRT-0116)  70.6 %   1 h 30
  main                        fp    no                3,705 gcells overflow (allowed)   64.8 %   ~2 h 40
  b                           0.1   no                0 overflow                       57.8 %   55 min
  b (final)                   0.1   yes               0 overflow                       64.6 %   22 min
  c                           0.5   yes               met2 demand 121.9 % of capacity, 357,228 overflowed gcells (allowed)
  d                           0.3   yes               met2 86.9 %, 71,412 overflowed gcells (allowed)
  c and d then failed in detailed routing with DRT-0218 "Guide is not
  connected to design" on std-cell-only nets (e.g. net29359: buf_4 ->
  50 edfxtp DE pins; no macro pins), the usual result of routing
  guides from a heavily overflowed global route.

== Detailed routing (b: adj 0.1, macro blockages, 0 GRT overflow)
  iteration 0: 1,036,832 violations (met1 short 598,443; met2 short
    176,233; met1 spacing 92,570; ...), 52 min with 8 threads
  iteration 1: 842,148 violations (met1 short 546,723; met2 short 119,323)
  iteration 2: 833,572 after 30 % of the iteration (stopped)
  Without the met1-met3 macro blockages: 1,044,616 after iteration 0.
  The violations are signal-signal (net:net) met1/met2 shorts across
  the standard-cell area, not macro or PDN conflicts.

== Routing demand (blocking cause)
  The placed design needs ~1.2-1.3 M met2 and ~1.2-1.4 M met1 track-gcells
  of global routing (34.8-37.1 m of wire, 337k nets) in a 10 mm^2 die. At the ORFS sky130hd default derating (0.5), global
  routing needs 122 % of the met2 capacity; it only fits when the
  derating is lowered to 0.1, and detailed routing cannot realize those
  guides. The sky130 OpenRAM macros (29 % of the core) block met1-met3
  for routing. Reaching the derating ORFS sky130hd designs route at
  needs roughly 1.5-2x the routing area, i.e. a smaller design or a die
  larger than the Caravel user area.
